/-!
# Generators of prime-power circular units

This file provides factorization, valuation, and generation theorems for prime-power circular
units. For a prime `p` and a `p ^ (k + 1)`-th cyclotomic field `K / ℚ` with primitive root of
unity `ζ`, we establish the factorization of `1 - ζ ^ (b * p ^ r)` (`r ≤ k + 1`) into `p ^ r`
differences, show that every primitive difference `ζ ^ b - 1` (`gcd(b, p ^ (k + 1)) = 1`) is a
uniformizer at the unique prime of `𝓞 K` above `p`, and prove that
`cyclotomicUnits K ζ (p ^ (k + 1))` is generated by `torsion K` together with the ratio units
`cyclotomicRatioUnit`.

For odd primes `p`, we define the smoothed real circular units
`smoothedCyclotomicUnit` (`γ(b) = ζ ^ (h * (1 - b)) * (ζ ^ b - 1) / (ζ - 1)` for any `h` with
`2 * h ≡ 1 [ZMOD p ^ (k + 1)]`), establish their representative independence, values at `±1`,
congruence invariance, and Galois cocycle law `γ(b * c) = σ_c(γ(b)) * γ(c)`, and prove that they
generate `realCyclotomicUnits` (including cyclic generation over `Gal(K⁺ / ℚ)` from a lift of a
generator of `(ZMod (p ^ (k + 1)))ˣ`).

For `p = 2` and `a = k + 2 ≥ 2`, we define the dyadic smoothed real circular units
`dyadicSmoothedCyclotomicUnit` (`γ(b) = ζ ^ ((1 - b) / 2) * (ζ ^ b - 1) / (ζ - 1)` for odd `b`),
establish their values at `±1`, and prove that together with `-1` they generate
`realCyclotomicUnits`.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.smoothedCyclotomicUnit`: the real circular unit
  `ζ ^ (h * (1 - b)) * (ζ ^ b - 1) / (ζ - 1)` in `(𝓞 K⁺)ˣ` for odd `p` and `2 * h ≡ 1 [ZMOD p^a]`.
* `TauCeti.dyadicSmoothedCyclotomicUnit`: the real circular unit
  `ζ ^ ((1 - b) / 2) * (ζ ^ b - 1) / (ζ - 1)` in `(𝓞 K⁺)ˣ` for `p = 2`, `a ≥ 2`, and odd `b`.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.primePowerDifference_factorization`: factorization of `1 - ζ ^ (b * p ^ r)` into
  `p ^ r` differences at level `p ^ a`.
* `TauCeti.primitiveDifference_primeValuation`: every primitive difference `ζ ^ b - 1` has
  valuation `WithZero.exp (-1)` at the unique prime above `p`.
* `TauCeti.cyclotomicUnits_eq_torsion_sup_closure_ratios`: `cyclotomicUnits K ζ (p ^ (k + 1))` is
  generated by `torsion K` and the `cyclotomicRatioUnit`s.
* `TauCeti.smoothedCyclotomicUnit_mul`: Galois cocycle law `γ(b * c) = σ_c(γ(b)) * γ(c)`.
* `TauCeti.realCyclotomicUnits_eq_closure_smoothed` and
  `TauCeti.realCyclotomicUnits_eq_closure_dyadicSmoothed`: real circular units are generated by
  `-1` and the smoothed real generators.
* `TauCeti.realCyclotomicUnits_eq_closure_galoisOrbit` and
  `TauCeti.exists_cyclic_generator_realCyclotomicUnits`: cyclic generation of `realCyclotomicUnits`
  over `Gal(K⁺/ℚ)` for odd `p`.

## References

* L. C. Washington, *Introduction to Cyclotomic Fields*, Chapter 8.
* R. Sharifi, *Iwasawa Theory*, §§4.2–4.3, 4.7.
-/

